      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure `certified` is the right word here. To me, it implies that some formal certification or validation process has been completed.\n\nThis has been tested as much as any other feature in before being submitted, but \"certified\" seems to glorify that testing process a bit too much.\n\nCan you consider simplifying this to say something like:\n\n```\nGerrit 3.15 introduces production-ready support for repositories using Git\u0027s reftable reference\nstorage format, following improvements to stability and repository conversion.\n```",
