      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T19:29:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I find \"predictable fixed time execution\" is a bit too strong. It sounds like \"constant time\" to me.\nThe execution time still depends on factors such as the number of refs being updated, compaction, etc.\n\nThe [reftable documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/reftable) states:\n\n```\nSupport atomic push with O(size_of_update) operations.\n```\n\nnot strictly `O(1)`.\n\n\nCould we just state that performance scales much better as the number of refs grows?\n\n```suggestion\nautomatic compaction of refdb files. This integration significantly improves the scalability\nof reference lookups and updates, helping repositories with millions of refs maintain\nconsistent and predictable performance.\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 62,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "aeddccc5e93192dc661130f2bb22f5dc8fe8e630",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
